WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:11.200
Is there anything more satisfying in CS:GO that landing a crisp, clean bullet to the dome?

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.300
Well... maybe getting out of Silver,

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.860
I wouldn’t know.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:20.820
I’m Colin for theScore esports and this week on Top 10 we're talking all about headshots baby.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.460
Now, there's been six years of competitive CS:GO.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:30.540
That's six years of melon-melting, armor-piercing headshots.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.720
And picking the 10 of those was nearly impossible.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:39.360
But we did it anyway. So from to pistols to AWPs, wallbangs to one-taps,

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.280
here are the Top 10 Headsho- f--k

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:46.860
here are the Top 10 Headshots in CS:GO

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:55.220
The first play on our list is a historic ace from EnvyUs’ Happy at Dreamhack Open London 2015.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:01:00.740
After four beautiful headshots, and one slightly less beautiful kill, later Happy  earned

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:04.320
himself a permanent spot in CS GO history.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:25.360
(Casting)

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:33.740
Coming in at number 9 is the, now infamous, Bodyy wallbangs against Astralis during ESL Proleague S5.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:41.960
Bodyy manages to hit not one but two headshots, through the wall, from spawn, in one map.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.480
Shots so insane that Valve actually had to patch them out of the game.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:02:24.760
(Casting)

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:30.240
The number 8 play on our list puts the spotlight on Fnatic’s olofmeister, who absolutely

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:36.780
dismantled NA’VI in a 1v5 at ESL One Katowice 2015.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:42.240
Oh yeah, and he did it with four back-to-back Tec 9 Headshots.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:03:09.320
(Casting)

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:16.720
At number 7 is a creative play from NiP’s GeT_RiGhT in the losers bracket final of StarSeries season 12.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:23.380
Getting a boost from allu, GeT_RiGhT hits an absolutely disgusting mid air headshot

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:25.440
with the Tec 9 on Device...

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.220
that just shouldn't be possible.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:49.880
(Casting)

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:56.220
Back at it again at number 6 is GeT_RiGhT, this time at the ESL Proleague Season 4 semifinals.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:02.160
GeT_RiGhT shows off his laser focus with this near instant flick onto Fer.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:05.880
Hitting this wallbang headshot with the narrowest of margins.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:16.240
(Casting)

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:23.320
Coming in at number 5 is a play that comes from Dreamhack Open Cluj 2015’s closed qualifier.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:29.340
Adren managed to secure this insane 4k clutch to win this round against Wizards with the

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:36.400
final kill coming from a VAC-worthy 180 degree flick to some poor soul’s face.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:49.340
(Casting)

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.620
ScreaM is a name synonymous with one taps.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:58.500
In our number 4 play from CS Summit 2017 he didn’t even have the luxury of the second

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:03.920
chance but still managed to connect his lone AK bullet with Fer’s melon.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:12.160
(Casting)

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.230
One headshot is nice.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.220
Two is impressive.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:19.960
Three is nearly super-human.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:24.800
But four? What in God’s name is this play from Snax.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:06:02.880
(Casting)

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.800
How do you top 4 back-to-back headshots?

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:16.100
Well, try five, with our runner up play from EnvyUs’ XMS at the PGL Europe Minor Championship 2017.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:22.780
XMS melts all five members of Team Kinguin with only five bullets.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:58.100
(Casting)

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:03.580
Taking the top spot on our list is a play that has etched itself in CS:GO history.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:08.600
We’ve all seen it a million times and it ages like a fine wine.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:14.240
So sit back and watch in awe at Hiko’s still inhuman reaction.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:47.680
(Casting)

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.080
Well guys that’s our list for this week.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:55.460
Now if you do disagree with it, I advise to load up an aim and practice your head shots.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.780
Don’t even comment, don’t @ me.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:58.880
I don’t want to hear it,

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:05.540
Thanks for watching. If you want more great content just like this, be sure to hit the subscribe button.

